CMakeUserPresets.json

# Build directories
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# CMake generated
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
*.cmake
!CMakeLists.txt
# ...but cmake/ holds SOURCE scripts, not generated ones — the MinGW toolchain
# file and the resource-embed script both live there, and both are named on a
# command line rather than being generated. Without this negation the blanket
# *.cmake above keeps them out of a fresh clone, and the Windows build and the
# self-contained standalone are each unreproducible. Both parent projects had to
# fix exactly this. Generated .cmake files all live under the build directories
# already ignored above.
#
# TWO forms, and the second is what this repository's shape costs. A gitignore
# pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding the .gitignore,
# so "!cmake/*.cmake" negates the root cmake/ and NOTHING ELSE — the moment the
# products' own cmake/ directories moved under products/, a new file in either
# of them became silently invisible to git add. Measured with git check-ignore,
# not assumed. The "**/" form is what reaches them at any depth.
!cmake/*.cmake
!**/cmake/*.cmake

